  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Port deferred convex/composite work lists, PFM manifold dispatch, three sort-key stages and per-pair contact reduction.",
  "regressions": [
    "Six stage contracts each retain seven live native cases, including all 81 shape-tag pairs over seven pose profiles, tails, mixed same-body filtering, both composite orientations and overflow.",
    "Native candidate supersets validate nondeterministic atomic membership and legal overflow subsets without feeding host physics into kernels.",
    "Composite input validation rejects cycles, invalid primitive ranges and repeated leaf identities; exact guards and native-copy reduction remain required.",
    "The triangle fallback regression from 0047 remains required by the PFM contract."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "NarrowPhasePfmPair fields are public for alternate backend interop, allowing direct native offset export; its repr(C) layout and physics are unchanged.",
    "Shape compute_aabb shares its existing arithmetic with an explicit-pose adapter for composite traversal and native local_extent. Signed local shape selectors avoid a pinned compiler unsigned negative-bound failure.",
    "BVH leaf sentinel bits are reinterpreted as signed -1 locally; out-of-range exit sentinels terminate exactly as the native bounded traversal.",
    "PFM deduplication may retain different finite inactive slots after its public count. Those payloads are reported but not compared as contacts; padding, inactive record tails, counts and active fields stay checked.",
    "Rust composite-composite collisions remain unsupported, and native secondary-witness clipping approximations remain explicit."
  ],
  "related_changes": [
    "0047-triangle-fallback-containment",
    "0046-convex-pfm-manifolds"
  ]
}
